{
  "dom_id": "step-q43509",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that an elementary matrix is obtained by performing exactly one elementary row operation on the identity matrix $I.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $P$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from $I$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $Q$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=7{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=7{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =Q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $S$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =S\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $Q$ and $S$ are elementary matrices.",
